        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most home mowers, an Oregon Gator G5 matched to your part number is the best single upgrade: it mulches better than stock, still bags well, and holds its edge longer. On a budget, a G3 or MaxPower 3-in-1 does the job; on a zero-turn mowed hard, the thicker G6 is worth its price.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, match the part number, fit it sail-up, check the balance and torque the bolt properly. Get those right and a new blade will make a bigger difference to your lawn than almost anything else you can spend the same money on.
          </p>
